QueryAST’s expand entries are defined as nested QueryAST objects (which require an `object` field). Here `expand()` defaults to `{}` when no subQuery is provided, producing an invalid nested query per the spec schema. Consider requiring subQuery to include `object`, or auto-populating it (e.g., from relation) so the generated AST validates.
```suggestion
   *
   * Note: Per the QueryAST spec, expand entries must be nested QueryAST objects
   * and therefore require an `object` field. We enforce that here to avoid
   * generating invalid ASTs.
   */
  expand(relation: string, subQuery?: Pick<QueryAST, 'object'> & Partial<QueryAST>): this {
    if (!subQuery || !subQuery.object) {
      throw new Error('expand() requires a subQuery with an `object` field to build a valid QueryAST.');
    }
    if (!this.query.expand) {
      this.query.expand = {};
    }
    (this.query.expand as Record<string, any>)[relation] = subQuery;
```

Spec route for object permissions is GET /api/v1/auth/permissions/:object (under auth prefix), but this client calls /api/v1/permissions/objects/:object. Update the path (and route base) to match the spec so the SDK is actually protocol-compliant.
```suggestion
      const route = this.getRoute('auth');
      const res = await this.fetch(`${this.baseUrl}${route}/permissions/${encodeURIComponent(object)}`);
```

i18n routes don’t match the spec defaults. Spec uses GET /api/v1/i18n/translations/:locale (path param) with optional query params, but this client calls /translations?locale=...; update to place locale in the path to match the REST registration.
```suggestion
      if (options?.namespace) params.set('namespace', options.namespace);
      if (options?.keys) params.set('keys', options.keys.join(','));
      const query = params.toString();
      const url = `${this.baseUrl}${route}/translations/${encodeURIComponent(locale)}${query ? `?${query}` : ''}`;
      const res = await this.fetch(url);
```

Spec defines i18n translations as GET /api/v1/i18n/translations/:locale (path param), but this test asserts /translations with locale as a query param. Update to match the spec route shape so the test validates correct client behavior.
```suggestion
        expect(url).toContain('/api/v1/i18n/translations/zh-CN');
        expect(url).toContain('/api/v1/i18n/translations');
```
